\section{Related Work}

\paragraph{Safe Robot Learning.}
VLA safety has emerged as a multifaceted challenge spanning training-time and inference-time defenses \citep{li2026vlasafety}. Inference-time methods include SDF-guided denoising \citep{song2026omniguide}, CBF-based trajectory projection \citep{hu2025aegis}, and CBF-embedded diffusion \citep{xiao2025safediffuser}; these offer robustness to novel obstacles but add latency and require runtime scene geometry. Training-time approaches such as SafeVLA \citep{zhang2025safevla} reduce safety cost via constrained policy optimization \citep{zhao2024scpo} but lack geometric grounding. CoFreeVLA \citep{zhai2026cofreevla} addresses dual-arm self-collision via a binary halt/continue risk estimator at inference time. \ours{} resolves a different tension: internalizing environment collision geometry into VLA weights for continuous geometric shaping with zero inference overhead.

\paragraph{Vision-Language-Action Models.}
RT-2 \citep{brohan2023rt2} pioneered the VLA paradigm by casting actions as language tokens, and OpenVLA \citep{kim2024openvla} provided an open-source autoregressive alternative; $\pi_0$ \citep{black2024pi0} introduced continuous flow-matching action generation, which $\pi_{0.5}$ \citep{black2025pi05} extended to open-world generalization with open-source weights via the openpi codebase. Recent work has explored geometric priors: GLaD \citep{guo2025glad} distills 3D geometric features into VLA hidden states for general spatial understanding, and GeoAware-VLA \citep{abouzeid2025geoaware} integrates frozen geometric vision features to improve viewpoint generalization. \ours{} differs in internalizing collision-specific SDF geometry into flow-matching weights for safety rather than general spatial robustness.

\paragraph{SDF in Robotics and Guidance Distillation.}
Signed distance representations have long been central to collision-free motion planning \citep{zucker2013chomp, schulman2014trajopt}. Neural SDF representations, pioneered by DeepSDF \citep{park2019deepsdf}, have since been adopted in manipulation planning \citep{chen2026cssdf,weng2023ngdf}, and several VLA works use a ``train-with-geometry, infer-without'' paradigm for general spatial accuracy \citep{liu2025occvla,li2025spatial,qian2025geopredict}. Separately, \citet{meng2023distillation} showed that classifier-free guidance can be distilled into diffusion model weights, and \citet{kim2026sgf} further establish that negative guidance in flow models \citep{lipman2023flow} must activate within a specific noise regime. \ours{} transfers these ideas to VLA safety: we internalize configuration-space SDF into flow-matching velocity fields through an auxiliary head discarded at inference, with a noise-aware weight $w(t)$ that instantiates the regime-specific activation principle for collision shaping.


