\subsection{Training Pipeline}
\label{sec:training}
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

\ours{} follows the standard $\pi_{0.5}$ fine-tuning pipeline. We perform full fine-tuning (not LoRA) with AdamW and DDP across two GPUs; complete training hyperparameters are provided in Appendix~\ref{app:training}. Gradients from both $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SDF}}$ and $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{col}}$ propagate through the shared features into the action expert weights (i.e., the SDF head's input features are not detached from the computation graph). This end-to-end gradient flow is the mechanism by which collision awareness becomes encoded in the velocity field. SDF labels cover ${\sim}$75\% of training tasks; samples without labels contribute only $\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{FM}}$.

